# Cartridge JSON is hash-pinned: an approved candidate is identified by the
# SHA-256 of its raw bytes, and the canonical copy under cartridges/ must stay
# byte-equivalent to its app-bundled mirror. On Windows, core.autocrlf=true
# smudges LF->CRLF at checkout, which changes those raw bytes (and so the
# SHA-256) without changing anything Git tracks. Pin these paths to LF so the
# approved hash survives checkout, clone and rebase on every platform.
#
# Deliberately scoped to the cartridge paths only -- not a repo-wide JSON
# policy.
cartridges/*.json text eol=lf
app/src/data/cartridges/*.json text eol=lf
